margins an sentinel lymph node  implant in place  s p 5 years of  Anastrozole  The patient has now discovered a nodule in upper inner quadrant of  the left breast  The patient is on low dose aspirin  she is not allergic to  lidocaine     Review of constitutional symptoms  generally feeling well     Physical Exam  Constitutional  The patient appeared well developed   well nourished  and in no acute distress   The left breast showed a 1cm non tender  well defined  round  firm  fixed  erythematous nodule in the upper outer quadrant     Ultrasound was used to evaluate the lesion and showed a 1 x 1 4cm lesion that  was ill defined  irregular  solid and cystic heterogeneously  hypoechoic without  significant internal vascularity     Assessment  Based on the clinical history and physical examination  an FNAB is  warranted     Procedure  The procedure and potential complications were explained to the  patient  who understood the purpose  risks  and benefits of the procedure  The  patient confirmed name  date of birth  laterality  and lesion to be aspirated   Written consent was obtained     The biopsy procedure was performed by palpation     2 aspirates were performed using 25 gauge needles with local anesthesia and  without complications   Slides were stained for immediate evaluation  Additional tissue was submitted  for further evaluation     The procedure was performed by  Rosemary Tambouret  M D     Disposition  The immediate interpretation was not discussed with the patient   Erin Sullivan  NP and Peter Goss  MD  were notified of the preliminary results  by e mail at 10 30 am         The signing pathologist attests that he she performed the procedure or  if  performed by a resident or fellow  directed and supervised the FNA procedure and  was immediately available to further assist the resident fellow before  during  and after the procedure  and has reviewed and confirmed the interpretation of  slides stained for immediate evaluation            Electronically Signed Ou