r cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 09 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm re excision specimen which is oriented with a short stitch anterior  long stitch lateral and bow cephalad  The specimen shows a cavity which opens toward the posterior aspect  The specimen is inked blue  anterior   black  posterior   green  superior   yellow  inferior   The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a smooth biopsy cavity measuring approximately 4cm in maximal diameter surrounded by fibrosed and adipose tissue  A firm fibrosed and suspicious area is identified at the medial margin  0 5cm away from the cavity  A second firm area is identified 0 5cm from the posterior margin in the lateral aspect of the cavity  Representative section is submitted as follows  A B  Samples from the medial area  C  Cavity towards anterior margin  3 0cm from the medial end  D  Cavity towards inferior  4cm from the medial margin  E  Cavity towards anterior  5 0cm from the medial end  F  Second mass at lateral edge  G  Adjacent to F  H  0 5cm from the lateral end of the cavity towards the posterior margin  K  Towards anterior margin  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  axillary sentinel nodes primary  973  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm node which is bivalved and submitted entirely in cassette I  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  secondary axillary sentinel node  120  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm lymph node which is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassette J  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  tertiary axillary sentinel node  111  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm lymph node which is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in L and M  Resident  MASSIMO D APUZZO  MD PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Kevin S  Hughes  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL 973   EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL 120   EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLRY SENTINEL 111   EXCISION PART D  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Positive.
