Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 56 CLINICAL DATA  Non palpable right breast cancer on sterotactic core from outside hospital                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU CONFINED TO THE MASS  SEE NOTE  BREAST  RIGHT    ADDITIONAL MARGIN   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 17 OF 17 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 19                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  number only is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of breast with a localizing needle and accompanying specimen X ray  Inked and sectioned to reveal a firm white stellate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm lesion extending to within 0 5cm of the closest inked margin  A representative section is frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  Sections of mass are submitted in cassettes A B  Representative sections of breast  submitted in cassettes C E  A portion of the lesion is taken by Dr  Deutch  Received in two container  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm aggregate mass of adipose tissue and lymph nodes  Lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes F through Q  Labeled  additional margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE unoriented piece of breast tissue  Sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes R through T  Resident  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT  PARTIAL MASTECTOMY PART B  RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES PART C  ROGHT BREAST  ADDITIONAL MARGIN   report_end  , Positive.
