laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 MAY 98 at 14 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two specimens  Labeled  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm simple mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm skin ellipse containing an unremarkable nipple aerolar complex and a 0 8cm in greatest dimension flesh colored papule located 2 0cm from the lateral side margin  Also present is a 2 0cm linear  well healed scar along the lateral side margin  The deep aspect of the specimen is inked in black while the anterior aspect of the specimen is inked in blue  Sectioning reveals predominantly fibrous parenchyma with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm biopsy cavity underlying the skin scar and located 0 5cm from the nearest  deep  margin  Scattered throughout the fibrous parenchyma are multiple foci of gritty  firm  clusters of punctate  tan white to brown areas ranging in size from 0 4cm to 1 5cm and located up to 0 3cm from the deep margin and abutting the anterior margin  The biopsy cavity is submitted entirely in cassettes A through C medial to lateral with closest margin and skin papule in B  Representative sections of the gritty areas are submitted in cassettes D through G with closest deep margin in E and closest anterior margin in G  The remaining breast parenchyma shows fibrocystic changes and representative sections have been submitted in H and I  Labeled  left axillary sentinel lymph node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm lymph node bivalved and entirely submitted in J  Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D            