eptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 06 59 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3cm fragment of fibroadipose breast parenchyma with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 1cm skin ellipse  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 2cm firm  tan white mass with abundant mucus that grossly extends 0 1cm from the inked margin as well as 1 5cm from the deep inked margin  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A B  Sections of tumor with closest inked margin  C  Representative sections of deep margin  D E  Representative sections of the mass  F  Representative sections of overlying skin ellipse  NOTE  A representative portion of the tissue is submitted for possible electron microscopy  and a photo taken  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   INVASIVE CARCINOMA  PROBABLY MUCINOUS  MARGIN GROSSLY FREE OF TUMOR  O R  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISION   report_end  , Negative.
