Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  28 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 55 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  MUCINOUS CARCINOMA  HYPOCELLULAR COLLOID TYPE   REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE MARGINS WITH BROAD FRONTS  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES  EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE TUMOR  PRESENT AT MARGINS  NOTE  No lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION OF ADDITIONAL MARGIN  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 42                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone 